    "sourceDescription": "About the Role F6 Ventures is seeking a highly analytical and operations-oriented Investment Analyst to support data-driven decision-making across our portfolio and fund activities. This is a core role focused on collecting, organizing, and analyzing quantitative and qualitative data from portfolio companies, supporting deal execution, and enhancing the fund’s internal systems and reporting infrastructure. Ideal for a candidate with a strong foundation in financial modeling, business analytics, and operational reporting, who thrives on precision, consistency, and visibility across portfolio performance. Key Responsibilities Portfolio Analytics & Reporting Maintain accurate, real-time dashboards that track key portfolio company KPIs, including MRR, ARR, burn rate, runway, CAC, LTV, active users, and cash balances. Produce monthly and quarterly performance reports for internal stakeholders, LPs, and investment committees. Calculate fund-level and company-specific return metrics including IRR, MOIC, DPI, and TVPI. Standardize and automate reporting across portfolio companies to ensure a consistent, high-quality data flow. Financial Modeling & Deal Support Build financial models and forecasts for existing and prospective portfolio companies. Perform sensitivity analyses, scenario planning, and valuation work to support investment decisions. Support due diligence by reviewing financial statements, projections, and deal terms. Assist in drafting investment memos and internal documentation. Fund Operations & Systems Support in managing equity positions, cap tables, and share movements for the fund and co-investors. Ensure accuracy across internal systems for investment tracking, CRM entries, and reporting tools. Coordinate with legal counsel and founders to ensure transactional documents are complete and reflect agreed terms. Support fund administration tasks, including data room management, compliance documentation, and investor deliverables. Fundraising & Follow-On Rounds Track follow-on fundraising rounds for portfolio companies, including round sizes, valuations, and the implications of dilution. Assist in preparing fundraising materials for future F6 Ventures funds (deck development, data compilation, and investor pipeline tracking). Provide analytical and operational support for LP engagement and roadshows. Market Research & Benchmarking Conduct benchmarking analyses across comparable startups and sectors. Monitor macroeconomic, regional, and sector-specific trends to support investment theses and internal prioritization. Support the creation of internal research reports on sectors of interest. Profile Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in finance, economics or a related field. 0–2 years of experience in venture capital, private equity, investment banking or corporate finance. Strong command of Google Sheets/Excel and financial modeling. Familiarity with the venture capital ecosystem and regional context is strongly preferred. Meticulous attention to detail with a high level of accountability in data integrity. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English & Arabic Comfortable working across multiple concurrent workstreams in a fast-paced environment. What We Offer Get the chance to work with high potential for growth startups and bright entrepreneurs Exposure to different local, regional and international investors and VCs Engage in the buzzing startup community in the MEA region Be part of a dynamic, c ollaborative, execution-focused team with regional reach and global ambition. F6.VC",
